  "gloss": "to run over; to hit (with a vehicle)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to run over; to hit (with a vehicle)",
      "explanation": "For a vehicle to strike a person or animal and pass over them. Always refers to a vehicle causing injury or death."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27775_hiku_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{車|くるま}→車：00516_kuruma⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{猫|ねこ}→猫：02237_neko⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{轢|ひ}いた。",
      "english": "A car ran over a cat.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27775_hiku_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{轢|ひ}いてしまわないよう⟦{慎重|しんちょう}→慎重：03264_shinchou⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{運転|うんてん}する→運転する：20318_untensuru⟧。",
      "english": "I drive carefully so as not to run anyone over.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27775_hiku_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦{道|みち}→道：00505_michi⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{飛|と}び{出|だ}して→飛び出す：02374_tobidasu⟧きた⟦{子供|こども}→子供：00554_kodomo⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{危|あや}うく→危うい：11825_ayaui⟧{轢|ひ}きそうになった。",
      "english": "I nearly ran over a child who darted out into the road.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive godan verb. X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{轢|ひ}く. Always describes a vehicle hitting a person or animal.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{轢|ひ}く: to run over a person\n- ⟦{車|くるま}→車：00516_kuruma⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{轢|ひ}かれる: to be hit by a car (passive)\n- {轢|ひ}き{逃|に}げ: hit-and-run\n\nUSAGE:\n{轢|ひ}く shares its reading with ⟦{引|ひ}く→引く：01978_hiku⟧ (to pull), ⟦{弾|ひ}く→弾く：02444_hiku⟧ (to play a stringed instrument), and ⟦{挽|ひ}く→挽く：12794_hiku⟧ (to grind), but is written with its own kanji and used only for vehicle accidents.",
